     "text": "```json\n{\"count\": 1, \"rationale\": \"With no defences the attack succeeds, so at least one control is needed. Without defences: phishing gives foothold_workstation and stolen_user, pivot_internal gives reach_internal, auth_appserver then kerberoast_dc gives stolen_admin, auth_dc then escalate_dc then dump_dbadmin_dc gives stolen_dbadmin, and auth_db then escalate_db then exfiltrate_db gives exfiltrated. Deploying mfa:admin alone stops this. The only sources of stolen_dbadmin are dump_dbadmin_dc (needs admin_dc) and dump_dbadmin_adfs (needs admin_adfs). Those need foothold_dc or foothold_adfs, which only auth_dc and auth_adfs give, and both require NOT mfa_admin. Without stolen_dbadmin, auth_db, auth_fileserver and auth_backup cannot fire. So no foothold or admin is possible on db, fileserver or backup, and none of the three exfiltrate techniques can run. Minimum is 1.\"}\n```"
    }
